  "notes": [
    "The left panel every page wears (the public site, the Products page, the account screen, the products). One source: a page renders these groups in this order, then its own group and 'On this page'.",
    "An entry with 'pane' names a section of the site's home page (the address is the site plus '#' and the pane); 'step' numbers the Get started steps; 'action' is a control the page provides (the Email Admin dialog); 'sub' nests labelled sub-groups inside an entry.",
    "A group with 'roles' is carried hidden and shown by the shell script when /__hub/session on the page's own origin answers with a user holding one of those roles. The Account group shows the visitor's name and Sign out for any signed-in visitor.",
    "Job Search views (?view=...) open at the Job Search address the page knows: the public short path here; a page served on the loopback derives them from its directory (apps/hub-portal/src/links.ts).",
    "A sub-group whose id is 'data' (Admin > Data management) is folded: its row is closed until pressed, open on its own pages, and closes again when another entry is chosen; it carries the data accent."
  ],
